<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42394" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρᾱτύω</span></b> , impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρήτυον</span> (without augm.) <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			18.503
		</span></i>, 
			Ion.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1301
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				11.341
			</span></i> : fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.296
				</span></i>
			, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1416
			</span></i>(anap.): aor. 1 opt. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύσειε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.192
				</span></i>
			, imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρήτυσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1260
				</span></i>
			, Iterat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύσασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.189
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.567
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.75
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			 (v. infr.). [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span>
			before a vowel, unless it be a long syll., as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητῡοντο μένοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.345
				</span></i>
			 (exc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρατύει <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span></span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				164
			</span></i> (lyr.)); long before <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς</span>, and in
				3pl.
			aor. 1
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρήτῡθεν.</span>]:—
				Ep.
			Verb (used twice in Trag.), <i>restrain, check,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήρυκες δ᾽ ἄρα λαὸν ἐρήτυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.503
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύσασκε φάλαγγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.567
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέεσσιν ἐρήτυε φῶτα ἕκαστον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.164
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.493
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύσειέ τε θυμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.192
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ κέλευθος ἐρατύει</span>
			a long road <i>parts</i> us, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
			</span></i>l.c. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρατύοι</span> Musgr.):—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύοντό τε λαόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.723
				</span></i>
			 : —
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ νηυσὶν ἐρητύοντο μένοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.345
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρητύετ᾽ ἐν φρεσὶ θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.462
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρήτυθεν</span>
				(3pl.) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὲ καθ᾽ ἕδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.99
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				211
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later c.
			gen., <i>to keep away from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνα δεινῆς ἁμίλλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1260
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[κύνας] ὑλαγμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.75
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ κακότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.296
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυτιλίης ..ἐρητύοντο μέλεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.835
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c.
			inf., <i>prevent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὰ μίμνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					14.63
				</span></i>
			.</div>
